---
import BaseLayout from '~/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocsShell from '~/components/DocsShell.astro';
import CodeBlock from '~/components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '~/components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE, VERSIONS } from '~/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Teptris Rust — TOML docs"
  description="The teptris crate: TOML 1.1 for Rust over libteptris — loads/dump/dump_json_natural, hand-maintained FFI, engine-linked, 7-45x the toml crate on loads."
>
  <DocsShell
    crumb="Teptris — Rust"
    title={`Teptris — the crate v${VERSIONS.tomlRs}`}
    lede={`Hand-maintained FFI over libteptris v${VERSIONS.toml} — no bindgen, no fallback. The safe API materializes the whole tree into an owned Value with insertion-ordered tables and real datetime fields; the engine's margin passes through almost intact.`}
  >
    <h2 id="install">Installation</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`cargo add teptris`} />
    <p>
      The crate is source + link directives: your build needs
      <code>libteptris</code> available and your runtime needs it
      findable (the binding is dynamically linked — the engine is not
      bundled). Install the engine (<code>cmake --install</code> puts
      it on the default loader path), or point
      <code>TEPTRIS_LIB_PATH</code> at a directory containing
      <code>libteptris.&#123;dylib,so,dll&#125;</code>. The
      <code>teptris-descriptor</code> companion crate ships the
      no_std shared descriptor-plan ABI.
    </p>

    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="rust"
      code={`use teptris::{loads, dump, dump_json_natural, Value};

let v = loads(b"name = \\"demo\\"\\nport = 8080\\n").unwrap();
assert_eq!(v.get("name").and_then(Value::as_str), Some("demo"));

let toml = dump(&v).unwrap();        // canonical; parse(dump(v)) == v
let json = dump_json_natural(&v).unwrap();
// real numbers, booleans, RFC 3339 datetime strings,
// non-finite floats as null — the host JSON view`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Document::parse</code> returns the zero-copy-managed
      document with <code>to_toml_string</code>,
      <code>to_json_string</code> (the toml-test conformance dialect)
      and <code>to_json_natural_string</code>. <code>ParseError</code>
      carries the message plus 1-based <code>line</code>/
      <code>column</code>.
    </p>
    <Callout kind="note">
      <p>
        <code>teptris_parse</code> NUL-terminates strings in the input
        buffer, so the safe <code>Document</code> owns a writable copy
        of its input for its lifetime;
        <code>Document::parse_buf(Vec&lt;u8&gt;)</code> takes ownership
        without the extra copy.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <h2 id="descriptor">Descriptor plans</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="rust"
      code={`use teptris::plan::{Descriptor, PlanRow};

let d = Descriptor::build(&[
    PlanRow::scalar("title"),
    PlanRow::collection("tags"),
    PlanRow::nested("owner", vec![
        PlanRow::scalar("name"),
        PlanRow::raw("meta"),
    ]),
])?;

let doc = teptris::Document::parse(b"title = \"d\"\n[owner]\nname = \"r\"\n")?;
let v = d.walk(&doc)?; // only planned keys materialize`}
    />
    <p>
      Compile a plan once, walk any number of documents in ONE native
      pass — unplanned keys are never materialized. MISSING rows are
      absent (rust has no null); <code>raw</code> rows re-use the plain
      node accessors on the untouched subtree.
    </p>

    <h2 id="performance">Performance</h2>
    <p>
      Against <strong>toml 0.8</strong> (the ecosystem standard,
      serde-based) over the engine bench corpus:
      <strong>7–45× faster on loads</strong> — datetime-heavy shapes
      3.79 ms vs 168.89 ms, integer-heavy 6.25 ms vs 278.52 ms — and
      <strong>3–8× on dumps</strong>. It is the widest gap of any tier
      the family measures: there is no language-boundary tax
      comparable to the wasm bridge, so the C engine&rsquo;s margin
      passes through intact. The lane runs in CI
      (<code>cargo bench --bench tier</code>, report-only).
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href={`${SITE.githubTomlRs}`}>Source — teptris-rs</a>.
    </p>
  </DocsShell>
</BaseLayout>
